    Drop the unused release tag workflow (#8176)
    
    The "Cut Release Tag" workflow was added in 2022 to automate cutting a
    release from the GitHub Actions user interface. It has never produced a
    release: no tag in the repository was created by it, and the release
    manager documentation never referred to it.
    
    It also cannot work any more. The checkout does not fetch the submodules
    the root pom.xml has listed since March 2026, so the build fails at
    once. The script calls the standalone docker-compose binary, which the
    Ubuntu 24.04 runner image no longer ships. The tag it would push is
    unsigned and pushed with the workflow token, which triggers neither the
    release build nor the Matrix room update. And the documented process
    meanwhile also tags the three submodule repositories, which the script
    knows nothing about.
    
    Rather than carry a dead workflow, remove it. Release automation can be
    rebuilt against the current documented procedure if wanted.
    
